WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.220
Documentation is part of the trust evidence for a model, not a courtesy added after the technical work is finished.

2
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:21.160
A useful model record should help future users and reviewers understand origin, intended use, limitations, training or fine-tuning context, evaluation notes, license terms, ownership, and operational constraints.

3
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.160
Model cards and similar records are valuable because they make assumptions explicit.

4
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:35.940
They can explain what the model was built for, what it was not built for, what data sources shaped it, how it was evaluated, and what known limitations should influence deployment decisions.

5
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.880
That context helps prevent overuse outside the intended workflow.

6
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.840
Dataset information matters.

7
00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:53.300
Training and fine-tuning sources can affect quality, policy fit, compliance expectations, bias concerns, confidentiality assumptions, and user communication.

8
00:00:53.400 --> 00:01:01.480
Even when dataset details are incomplete, the record should describe what is known, what is unknown, and how uncertainty affects approval.

9
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:07.040
License review should happen before a checkpoint is approved for shared use or commercial workflows.

10
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:17.380
A model may be technically useful while still having terms that restrict redistribution, hosted use, derived work, attribution, or particular operating contexts.

11
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:22.680
License uncertainty should be visible instead of hidden in a download note.

12
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.800
Ownership should also be clear.

13
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:31.220
Someone should know who approved the model, who maintains it, who can change it, and who can retire it.

14
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:40.280
Missing documentation should lower confidence and trigger a more cautious intake path, because undocumented trust is difficult to defend when something changes.
